# Verso — device-type icons keyed by MAC OUI (the IEEE Organizationally Unique
# Identifier: the first three octets of a MAC address).
#
# Format mirrors nmap-mac-prefixes for familiarity and tooling compatibility:
#   <OUI> <icon> <vendor>
# OUI is six uppercase hex digits; <icon> must be a name defined in
# internal/widget/icons.go; the trailing <vendor> is a human label the resolver
# ignores. Blank lines and lines beginning with '#' are ignored.
#
# This is a deliberately TIGHT, curated seed: only vendors whose devices use a
# real (non-randomized) MAC and map cleanly to a single device type. Multi-
# product vendors (Apple, Samsung, Amazon, Google) are intentionally absent —
# their OUI says nothing about the device kind, so they resolve via hostname
# (see hostname-icons) or fall back to the generic icon. A locally-administered
# (randomized) MAC never matches here by design.
#
# Contributions welcome: add a line for a vendor whose devices are one
# recognisable kind. Seeded from the IEEE registry via nmap-mac-prefixes.
#
